Item 2. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Results of Operations and Financial Condition.
This analysis should be read in conjunction with the condensed consolidated financial statements and the notes thereto.
Results of Operations
The Company reported net income attributable to common shares of $281.1 million ($64.86 per share) for the second quarter of 2026, compared to $36.7 million ($8.35 per share) for the second quarter of 2025.
Items included in the Company’s net income for the second quarter of 2026:
•a $137.0 million settlement gain related to a retiree annuity pension purchase (after-tax impact of $101.3 million, or $23.38 per share);
•$3.8 million in non-operating expenses related to Separation Incentive Programs (SIPs) and a Voluntary Retirement Incentive Program (VRIP) at the education, television broadcasting and manufacturing divisions, and other businesses (after-tax impact of $2.8 million, or $0.66 per share);
•$0.2 million in interest income to adjust the fair value of the mandatorily redeemable noncontrolling interest (after-tax impact of $0.2 million, or $0.05 per share);
